    "essay": "Motivation in the workplace has been widely studied by researchers such as Maslow (1943) and Herzberg (1959). Maslow proposed a hierarchy of needs suggesting that employees are motivated by fulfilling basic needs before higher ones. Herzberg identified hygiene factors and motivators as separate influences on employee satisfaction. Based on these theories it is clear that financial incentives are the most effective way to motivate all employees in every organizational context. Organizations should therefore focus exclusively on salary increases and bonuses to improve employee performance. In conclusion the evidence from Maslow and Herzberg confirms that financial rewards are universally superior to all other motivational approaches."
